{{!--
  Maintainer notes (not emitted in G-code):
  - 4-axis Grbl post for Makera Carvera + rotary 4th-axis attachment.
  - A axis is the rotary axis (rotation around X by default on Carvera).
  - Lines starting with ";" are operator-visible comments in output.
  - Template context keys: resources/posts/README.md (PostContext / renderPost).
  - Additional context for 4-axis: axisCount, aAxisRangeDeg, aAxisOrientation.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  HISTORY / ROLE
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  This file was renamed from `cnc_4axis_grbl.hbs` to `carvera_4axis_grbl.hbs`
  (pre-launch punch-list rank 16) to reflect what it actually is. The "grbl"
  suffix is retained because the schema dialect enum entry is `grbl_4axis`,
  but the template family is Carvera-flavored Smoothieware -- the same
  dialect parent as the production `carvera_4axis.hbs` post (both emit
  Smoothieware-compatible 4-axis G-code using G21 / G90 / G17, M3 / M5
  spindle, A-axis rotation around X).

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  CPS DIALECT-COLLAPSE FALLBACK (April 2026)
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The April-2026 4-axis subsystem rewrite collapsed every non-GRBL 4-axis
  post template. The deleted templates were:

      cnc_4axis_fanuc.hbs        cnc_4axis_mach3.hbs
      cnc_4axis_linuxcnc.hbs     cnc_4axis_siemens.hbs
      cnc_4axis_heidenhain.hbs

  All five dialects (`fanuc_4axis` / `mach3_4axis` / `linuxcnc_4axis` /
  `siemens_4axis` / `heidenhain_4axis`) now route through THIS file via
  `src/main/machine-cps-import.ts` `postTemplateMap`. The dialect-enum
  entries are preserved in `src/shared/machine-schema.ts` so existing
  user machine profiles in %APPDATA%/WorkTrackCAM/machines/ still load
  (Safety Rule 2: never break saved projects). CPS-imported machines that
  declare those dialects emit Carvera/Smoothieware-compatible G-code, with
  a console warning from `machine-cps-import.ts` describing the fallback.

  Why "carvera_*" prefix is accurate: this template's invariants (G21 mm
  units, G90 absolute, G17 plane, M3/M5 spindle, A around X, M30 program
  end, semicolon comment style, no M6 ATC) match the Smoothieware family
  used by Makera Carvera. The 3-axis sibling is `carvera_3axis.hbs`; the
  production 4-axis post is `carvera_4axis.hbs`. This file is the
  *fallback* 4-axis post -- it covers CPS imports for foreign 4-axis
  dialects with output the Carvera can execute.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  SAFETY INVARIANTS
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Read `.claude/skills/gcode-safety/references/carvera-4axis.md` BEFORE
  editing this template. Key invariants that MUST hold in every render:
    - G21 / G90 / G17 in header (mm / absolute / XY plane).
    - `G0 Y0` in header before any feed move (centering on rotation axis;
      A rotates around X so tool must stay in the rotation plane).
    - No `M6` tool change emitted (rotary attachment occupies the ATC slot
      on Carvera; tool changes are operator-initiated via M0/M1 pause).
    - M5 spindle-off before final retract.
    - Final retract uses `G0 Z<workAreaZ>` then `G0 X0 Y0` park.
    - Program end via M30 (this template) -- `carvera_4axis.hbs` uses M2
      instead because Smoothieware community firmware may delete the file
      from SD on M30; this fallback template ships M30 because the legacy
      `grbl_4axis` dialect contract has emitted M30 since [ID-0156], and a
      unilateral switch here would change pinned snapshots. The Carvera
      production post is the safe path for actual Carvera hardware; this
      template is fallback-only for CPS-imported foreign dialects.

  Related contracts:
    - `src/main/post-process-carvera-4axis-contract.test.ts`
      (carvera_4axis.hbs contract pins)
    - `src/main/post-process-4axis-integration.test.ts`
      (this template integration coverage)
    - `src/main/post-process-dialect-safety.test.ts`
      (per-dialect header/footer pins)
--}}
; {{machine.name}} — {{machine.id}}
; 4-AXIS (A-ROTARY) G-CODE — grbl_4axis dialect
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; UNVERIFIED G-CODE — verify every line against your Carvera firmware docs
; and your rotary attachment manual before running on the machine.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; CRITICAL 4TH AXIS CHECKS BEFORE RUNNING:
; (1) Confirm the rotary attachment is firmly clamped to the table.
; (2) Confirm the workpiece is centred on the rotary chuck — off-centre
;     stock causes gouging and crashes.
; (3) Confirm cylinder diameter matches the value used to generate toolpaths.
; (4) Set A-axis WCS zero (usually the left face of the cylinder, A=0°).
; (5) Air-cut with spindle off at 10 % feed override before a real cut.
; (6) Confirm your Carvera firmware supports the A word in Grbl (some builds
;     require the rotary axis plugin — check Makera documentation).
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Retract order: lift Z to a safe radial clearance before commanding large A moves
; (toolpath lines already use clearance Z between passes; header retract is machine max Z).
; Before production: dry run — spindle off, Z high, feed reduced.
; Compare a short program to a known-good file from Makera CAM.
; See docs/MACHINES.md — safe Z, WCS, units, spindle M-codes.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Work area (mm): {{machine.workAreaMm.x}} x {{machine.workAreaMm.y}} x {{machine.workAreaMm.z}}
{{#if machine.aAxisRangeDeg}}; A-axis range: ±{{machine.aAxisRangeDeg}}° (verify against firmware soft limits)
{{/if}}
G21              ; millimeters — must match Carvera controller settings
G90              ; absolute distance mode (X Y Z A all absolute)
G17              ; XY plane for G2/G3 arcs; 4-axis arcs use XZ with G18 if needed
{{#if wcsLine}}; Active work offset — verify fixture zero matches G54–G59 selection
{{wcsLine}}
{{/if}}
{{#if operationLabel}}; Operation: {{operationLabel}}
{{/if}}; Home / safe position — retract Z before rotating A to avoid collisions
G0 Z{{machine.workAreaMm.z}} ; safe Z retract — adjust to your actual safe clearance
G0 Y0            ; CRITICAL: center tool on rotation axis (Y must be 0 for 4-axis rotary)
; Spindle on (Grbl — confirm S value matches your bit and material)
{{spindleOn}}
{{#if inverseTimeFeed}}; --- Inverse-time feed mode (G93) for continuous rotary axis motion ---
; F-word = 1/time (inverse minutes). Each G1 block must carry its own F value.
; G94 is restored after the toolpath to return to normal feed-per-minute mode.
; NOTE: Not all Grbl builds support G93. Verify your firmware supports it.
G93              ; inverse-time feed mode ON
{{/if}}; --- 4-axis toolpath moves begin (X Y Z A words) ---
{{#each toolpathLines}}
{{this}}
{{/each}}
; --- end toolpath ---
{{#if inverseTimeFeed}}G94              ; restore feed-per-minute mode
{{/if}}; Spindle off
{{spindleOff}}
; Retract Z to machine max clearance and park
; (Toolpath already returns A to 0° and retracts Z to clearance;
;  this final retract ensures the tool is at machine-max Z for unload.)
G0 Z{{machine.workAreaMm.z}} ; full retract for unload
G0 X0 Y0        ; park X, re-center Y on rotation axis
; M30 or M2 if your Grbl build supports program end (comment out if unsupported)
M30
